    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69865" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναυσθλόω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>carry by sea,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ γᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					162
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς γῆν πατρίδα ναυσθλώσων νεκρόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					1037
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i>take with one by sea,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναυσθλοῦσθε παῖδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>IT</u>
					1487
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>go by sea,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναυσθλοῦμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					677
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πελάγεσιν ναυσθλούμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1210
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ ναυσθλώσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					126
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be visited by ships,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ ναυσθλωθήσεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					1415
				</span></i>
			.</div>
